{"title":"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(No_Coordinates)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (No Coordinates)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Coord_bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Coord bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Menelaus,_Similarity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Menelaus, Similarity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f3f89572b856462928672098971109d030babbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=84$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/c/a0c4b6e70c9f6777aebe73c4203ec71abbc0740e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the trisection point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/e/cbeda7159b33badd3617a005290a98fb0be341cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CM}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95b477d09cebdb1d934aa42c671f090b161f430a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DN}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a202b0fb5674c4c38601ce5f884c5046fb8a866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCON$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4bb1db3d066da48df7576e30ef3831ec64cecc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BP}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> bisects the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a202b0fb5674c4c38601ce5f884c5046fb8a866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCON$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />. Find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7bc33a89a452917f2f02ab47639b75dcd266d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDP$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/7/5a74a61b8f16912c57c38674a47399d19a5d121e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,M,n,O,P; A=(0,42);B=(84,42);C=(84,0);D=(0,0);M=(0,21);n=(28,42);O=(12,18);P=(32,13); fill(C--D--P--cycle,blue); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(C--M); draw(D--n); draw(B--P); draw(D--P); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,W); label(&quot;$N$&quot;,n,N); label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,(-0.5,1)); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,N); dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(D); dot(M); dot(n); dot(O); dot(P); label(&quot;28&quot;,(0,42)--(28,42),N); label(&quot;56&quot;,(28,42)--(84,42),N); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"142\" />\nImpose a coordinate system on the diagram where point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the origin. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/8/1b8b506ac42fd69a41b8a03e1cd9080c84e2a459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(0,42)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/1669ee059917ab55ce1e68ab053f961283331073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=(84,42)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e983fcd17f1d8f3f535dd3c6fd77c6c3a9d76bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=(84,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c8bd013ea7bc3e200bdbb0adbdb7706c592787.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is a midpoint and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is a trisection point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb6fb77d1f669ab890885094e8eb2e57ba311eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=(0,21)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/790d136837e8bcfe0f88263e7c8a4ec5143d245a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=(28,42)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />. The equation for line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a816c89963674b87a98252a83530b78c7aa7aae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DN$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fb29ddb427e9b4a28a5d730d0ad088a2ae9364e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{3}{2}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"37\" /> and the equation for line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa38fd42cdaa5db0dd4e0f7df98ae79a598eb627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e493a9c6581f8c9710f1cefe882b535af16dbbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{84}x+\\frac{1}{21}y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"37\" />, so their intersection, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/7/b07e9ee3a0bbf3806d868e150a6ddc5c4d305cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(12,18)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />. Using the shoelace formula on quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a202b0fb5674c4c38601ce5f884c5046fb8a866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCON$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />, or drawing diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d29ab3cedcc24c862f97e5d7f2bb1da18b7067e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BO}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> and using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/26378ff876f01aea45dd3dd0a32b3db556e60cfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12bh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"31\" height=\"37\" />, we find that its area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d001b1c48658a4ba6e8323c63a4aac8ead76ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2184$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/3/0c33da4d16bf5f54ce503e3c1277199b0ff3b3d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCP$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/0/ca062f88e74d8fd2b8b5a0f55a4724dea0fc64ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2184}{2} = 1092$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"100\" height=\"37\" />. Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82991ecb63643f5330178e463fc72a75840174f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac 12 bh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"37\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bfb85211fca2f831753ba78372fc908eb12d609.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2184 = 42h$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />. Simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/6/27605f8beb26d5521a84936d71c1f0b30c6f31ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 52$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />. This means that the x-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/13014b9dd0ad42baef8ab26c278c64bb1341758f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = 84 - 52 = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"139\" height=\"13\" />. Since P lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e493a9c6581f8c9710f1cefe882b535af16dbbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{84}x+\\frac{1}{21}y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"37\" />, you can solve and get that the y-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/5/475c1750cd40aa671c95911512ff47f24201c3eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDP$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/c/eacaf7894902c12e819702e1b0a75e0aa47488e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 13 \\cdot 84=\\boxed{546}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"139\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28No_Coordinates.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(No_Coordinates)\">Solution 2 (No Coordinates)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (No Coordinates)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the problem tells us that segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4bb1db3d066da48df7576e30ef3831ec64cecc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BP}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> bisects the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a202b0fb5674c4c38601ce5f884c5046fb8a866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCON$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />, let us compute the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a202b0fb5674c4c38601ce5f884c5046fb8a866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCON$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> by subtracting the areas of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/d/f6de20e24bb4225633dda654847fe3d2986ee42a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AND}$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/8/fa87a09b70c6defbd443c3cfd113e0c2d2203161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{DOC}$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> from rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>To do this, drop altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25e374b1b3a5802e3fc77ff783bddb6c9c422b42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{OE}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> onto side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b7e5ec2db31e9aded4bb09881b42d1c439fce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and draw a segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/3/4c3a383fe381954061abbc53f28d399e3129d18d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"19\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3fdcb08ad6552495123aec5e4ba6b0ec9c9a0d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AN}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> from side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/e/c1e7a3d8baba2a89399aadb966789f5d3891cfc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{ND}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f4668ba4c04aaa65b65fb84c23757311f53db124.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overline{MQ}=14\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" /> Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25e374b1b3a5802e3fc77ff783bddb6c9c422b42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{OE}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90e6c10e06cdc3ccb720308752cdaec6decc6724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{MOQ}~\\triangle{COD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />, we can write the statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c62a727af4509b8d4a608b8e2846908fb110d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\overline{DC}}{a}=\\frac{\\overline{MQ}}{21-a}\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"40\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e8839e925d5f80333352c652c39ae4f799dfbbd0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\frac{84}{a}=\\frac{14}{21-a}\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7a03cca1f4543944c218740c705d476eec89eed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies a=18\\]\" width=\"89\" height=\"12\" /> Using this information, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/8/fa87a09b70c6defbd443c3cfd113e0c2d2203161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{DOC}$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/d/f6de20e24bb4225633dda654847fe3d2986ee42a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AND}$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/9/6f93b72d1391c6c6bc44b86b40580f3fe9a4fca1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{18\\cdot 84}{2}=756\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/2/4f2c6ec2bfc65dd7df60f59b180c1894e5d2b8f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{28\\cdot 42}{2}=588\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" /> respectively. Thus, the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a202b0fb5674c4c38601ce5f884c5046fb8a866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCON$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc3371da53b5a57ccbf32a99f49594374295fb3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[84\\cdot 42-588-756=2184\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"13\" /> Now, it is clear that point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6a5dab0650ea78f80ca12d62afe83905de42ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MC}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />, so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc9d50b6a07d3905fddb1cb09cc2983738c2ac8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{BPC}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6832559d81aa4d4fee88f31fd6e28be5ec1509.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2184}{2}=1092\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"37\" /> Given this, drop altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/4/5c4a3f5a777373e9e5825aaffdd2c1ac118c1df9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PF}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> (let's call it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />) onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e37cabcb7c85116bf5abd1af5ce7e4d31b1620cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{42b}{2}=1092\\implies b=52\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"37\" /> From here, drop an altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/8/f880e6f05c49291253112742fd634776728052d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PG}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b7e5ec2db31e9aded4bb09881b42d1c439fce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. Recognizing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/7/b3723199691cb1a6caac11dbb06ac5746b5c004b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PF}=\\overline{GC}$\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e1375c560a430b35f75d617e17a9afeb87347d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{MDC}$\" width=\"65\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/9/73941046e8d0b9c37bd5e278735b354244dc55fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{PGC}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> are similar, we write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fbd6c577bedca959c7809af60a02cb94b360095.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\overline{PG}}{\\overline{GC}}=\\frac{\\overline{MD}}{\\overline{DC}}\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fdad081d0ebf68db3aecaae69d0b1b49e22e1685.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\frac{\\overline{PG}}{52}=\\frac{21}{84}\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/f/24f006eb3c934c7652ea5e42676230e25ef6caf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\overline{PG}=13\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" /> The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/f/71f19e0fc89b34b358730439586c944c68e45d82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CDP}$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73b7829328da978539be8db69eadd451918c456.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\overline{DC}\\cdot \\overline{PG}}{2}=\\frac{84\\cdot 13}{2}=\\boxed{546}\\]\" width=\"214\" height=\"40\" /> ~blitzkrieg21 and jdong2006\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Coord_bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Coord_bash)\">Solution 3 (Coord bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Coord bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/109abc5be30e81335b3fb38da3cddd1ba09f9790.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = (0,0), C = (84,0), B = (84,42), A = (0,42)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"379\" height=\"20\" />. We can also find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/5/095bbdec1ec530354dd48d296d5529f9e7c2990b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = (0,21)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> by the midpoint formula. Now, lets find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/7/7778098e6f10ecdaf5eb74e56dcbfe099f22e785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ND$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa38fd42cdaa5db0dd4e0f7df98ae79a598eb627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />. So, we just need to find the equation of those lines, and solve. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a816c89963674b87a98252a83530b78c7aa7aae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DN$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, we first find the slope to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfc896328d9adffcde12a9ce948c480167401086.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{42}{28} = \\dfrac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" />. And obviously, the y-int is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So, our equation is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/1/7d1769680280d0667f285877d5614faf24576ec7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=\\dfrac{3}{2}x\\]\" width=\"56\" height=\"37\" />. Now, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa38fd42cdaa5db0dd4e0f7df98ae79a598eb627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />, we have a slope of: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed247e11e746432ae8aa947dd05e3317266e53a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{21}{-84} = -\\dfrac{1}{4}\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"37\" />, and the y-int is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so our equation is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfa7f91119c931a283dcbcc1739e31de40a04862.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=-\\dfrac{1}{4}x+21\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"37\" />, solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, we get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/7/b07e9ee3a0bbf3806d868e150a6ddc5c4d305cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(12,18)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />. Now, we use the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4bb1db3d066da48df7576e30ef3831ec64cecc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BP}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> bisects the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a202b0fb5674c4c38601ce5f884c5046fb8a866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCON$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />. By shoelace, we find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a202b0fb5674c4c38601ce5f884c5046fb8a866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCON$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d001b1c48658a4ba6e8323c63a4aac8ead76ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2184$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. Now, we will use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc9d50b6a07d3905fddb1cb09cc2983738c2ac8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{BPC}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. We have that its area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791afaad67c7c5a95a3f31d1c11fb15137836d61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2184}{2} = 1092$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"38\" />. So, by the area of a triangle formula the height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/3/0c33da4d16bf5f54ce503e3c1277199b0ff3b3d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCP$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. So, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e99a4a99e48f16c7d92a3e0712319215bb3ce327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84-52 = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />. Then, we use the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa38fd42cdaa5db0dd4e0f7df98ae79a598eb627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />, so using the equation of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa38fd42cdaa5db0dd4e0f7df98ae79a598eb627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> (which we found to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f6f4a8b98d3a5dfe5b5d00627abed201fb843b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\dfrac{1}{4}x+21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />, plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/7/c27f2ab499fe439b3b4da5e367aac50814010cb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=32$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/7/f0760e265c688498d8376016a70a86c33fc69c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />, so we have the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/4/6846f26cf40dee0ced4a8014756e1cb0b6dd9733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(32,13)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />, so the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0a0a4554dcbef4be00a35d49eff85301adc911b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PCD$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aed6e43f8a7456c9f6ce49d0b7c013c11710876f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{13\\cdot84}{2}=\\boxed{546}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~jb2015007\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Menelaus.2C_Similarity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Menelaus,_Similarity)\">Solution 4 (Menelaus, Similarity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Menelaus, Similarity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/d/edde6e01d0443068fb92133ac8c294aceff8dce3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(10cm); pair A = origin; pair B = (84, 0); pair C = (84, 42); pair D = (0, 42); pair M = (0, 21); pair N1 = (28, 0); pair O = (12, 24); pair P = (32, 29); pair X = (-84, 0);  draw(A--B--C--D--A--X--C); draw(B--P--D); draw(D--N1); draw(B--O);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, NW); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, NW); label(&quot;$N$&quot;, N1, S); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, NNE); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, N); label(&quot;$X$&quot;, X, SW); [/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"152\" />\nFrom the givens, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08f0caa91225579cab2b56950cf57af0c85ef89e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DM=MA=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"137\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/e/86effd35b146cd79a0b2bbc65e38b8ba712355a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN=28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33c60747f087e68501db30f2199fdba75872d75a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BN=56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />. Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> to meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa38fd42cdaa5db0dd4e0f7df98ae79a598eb627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/a/02aab9886d6cd41ed10eea0c40d2acf92a62f438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AXM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/3131fa30394dfcfe8d17e0cf55f181c1639920ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{DCM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> are congruent, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/9725c99991e69927854cc72ebe5a0f65a678b517.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX=84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />. From Menelaus' Theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59e31785d741742504c37b183bb326748f9f81a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{DAN}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd6661881018e056414533cad51376788fcc30b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{DM}{MA} \\cdot \\dfrac{AX}{NX}\\cdot \\dfrac{NO}{OD}=1.\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"37\" />\nAfter plugging in the known values, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/58296e5997c9fc30c66065dbb77d0be11f64bb91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{NO}{OD}=\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"39\" />. Let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be the point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/2/e8216bd52f56340385ff992817c47395285d599a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{DQO}\\sim\\triangle{DAN}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" />. Then, because of the ratio we just found, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0ead750aef63db2fcd6e40893000514fc1da213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QO=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, if we let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a86fd65190999580bd630c2d66545f4ebd07c6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q^{\\prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"19\" /> be the point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/4289c20e0f1737efd6114038ccaa0672385226e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ^{\\prime} \\parallel AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b35017e999bb6e32be4a4571384f92ba03a8678a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ^{\\prime}=72.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"19\" /> This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/4/614753af680f0b01158e935203b7fed8c4536bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[COB]=\\frac{1}{2}(72)(42).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"162\" height=\"38\" /> We can do the same process vertically to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4ea4e8acc2e77516f8783155678f50e611fcb1d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[NOB]=\\frac{1}{2}(24)(56)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"38\" />. Summing, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55e6bddc67139f9edcdf59318ca3a197ba759cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BCON]=12\\cdot 182$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0baf79d08b64f510fc8302d0e21f964af63db0fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[CPB]=6\\cdot 182$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/4/954b59f68715d6a48181e3a8e7dcacee9093c4fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Let the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Then, from similar triangles,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/6/5562e211e3af1dba6a6c536e1c9f3b0a0d0fbdef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{h}{21}=\\dfrac{52}{84}.\\]\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" />\nThis gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e62cd668613d118671619c2f02191079db0e1672.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, and thus the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/a/16acb2b10a5e381edb98dfe24d50e635b69d65d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(84)(13)=\\boxed{546}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"142\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>- The_Other_Guy\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II\" title=\"2017 AIME II\">2017 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2017\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018002458\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.070 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.090 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 924/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1808/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 130/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 30043/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.356      1 -total\n 59.11%    7.895      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.12%    5.092      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15521:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018002458 and revision id 281088. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}